Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:14:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: end the PC options submenu as soon as it has faded in

TYN-only: the Windows/Steam release of Memories Off 6 T-Wave opens the options
screen through the CC style submenu variables (SW_SYSSUBMENUNO 5,
SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA 0 -> 256) and never touches SW_OPTIONALPHA, which is what
the PS3 style MO6TW options menu is keyed on. The menu was therefore never
drawn while the script waited for SF_SUBMENUEXIT behind an invisible screen,
until the player happened to press Back.

The PS3 layout also does not fit the repacked PC option sheet (different
sliders, button sets and voice toggles), so showing it would only draw garbled
sprites. Until a PC specific options screen exists, raise SF_SUBMENUEXIT for
InstructionSet::MO6TWPC once the submenu alpha reaches 256: the script then
fades the submenu out and returns to the system menu list.

Observed on MuMu (Android 15): SW_SYSSUBMENUNO=5, SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA ramps
0..256 in steps of 16, SW_OPTIONALPHA stays 0 and no exit is ever raised.

diff --git a/src/games/mo6tw/optionsmenu.cpp b/src/games/mo6tw/optionsmenu.cpp
index a9875f4ed98b9e994d53182179cd7bc1bf42defb..552b70a123dfc1fd81abe458155b229bfe3c1d9d 100644
--- a/src/games/mo6tw/optionsmenu.cpp
+++ b/src/games/mo6tw/optionsmenu.cpp
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@
 #include "../../mem.h"
 #include "../../profile/scriptvars.h"
 #include "../../vm/interface/input.h"
+#include "../../vm/vm.h"
+#include "../../profile/vm.h"
 #include "../../audio/audiosystem.h"
 
 namespace Impacto {
@@ -343,6 +345,15 @@ void OptionsMenu::UpdateVisibility() {
 void OptionsMenu::Update(float dt) {
   UI::OptionsMenu::Update(dt);
 
+  // The PC scripts open the options screen through the CC style submenu variables (SW_SYSSUBMENUNO 5,
+  // SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA 0 -> 256) and never touch SW_OPTIONALPHA, so this PS3 layout is not shown (and its sprites do
+  // not match the repacked PC sheets anyway). Without an exit the script waits for SF_SUBMENUEXIT forever behind an
+  // invisible screen; end the submenu as soon as it has faded in so the game returns to the system menu flow.
+  if (Profile::Vm::GameInstructionSet == Vm::InstructionSet::MO6TWPC &&
+      ScrWork[SW_SYSSUBMENUNO] == 5 && ScrWork[SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA] == 256) {
+    SetFlag(SF_SUBMENUEXIT, true);
+  }
+
   if (State == Shown) {
     if (PADinputButtonWentDown & PAD1X)
       GoToPage((CurrentPage + 1) % Pages.size());
